Punctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Either the escaped prisoner was drowned crossing the river or he found his way across the border into Canada. [In any case], [he was never seen again].</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/8712.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Either the escaped prisoner was drowned crossing the river or he found his way across the border into Canada. &lt;b&gt;In any case&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;he was never seen again&lt;/b&gt;.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Are you looking for a holiday destination with sunshine, great food and beautiful scenery? [If so], [Majorca is the place for you].</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/8713.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Are you looking for a holiday destination with sunshine, great food and beautiful scenery? &lt;b&gt;If so&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;Majorca is the place for you&lt;/b&gt;.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The party went on much longer than I'd expected, and I didn't get home [until] [after four in the morning]. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/8714.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The party went on much longer than I'd expected, and I didn't get home &lt;b&gt;until after four in the morning&lt;/b&gt;. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I was sure I'd never been to the village before, [yet] [it looked strangely familiar].</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/8715.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I was sure I'd never been to the village before, &lt;b&gt;yet it looked strangely familiar&lt;/b&gt;.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>At first she looked at me with a furious expression on her face, but [soon] [she began to smile].</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/8716.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>At first she looked at me with a furious expression on her face, but &lt;b&gt;soon she began to smile&lt;/b&gt;.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The police had been unable to find sufficient evidence against her and, [therefore], [the trial could not go ahead].</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/8717.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The police had been unable to find sufficient evidence against her and, &lt;b&gt;therefore&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;the trial could not go ahead&lt;/b&gt;.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Pemberton leant forward and spoke quietly, [so that] [the others wouldn't hear].</text><label /><a